# PUSU live cron — DONCHIAN-ONLY (2026-06-16). Apply on VM: crontab dag/crontab (verify: crontab -l)
# All other streams retired (UI + DB + live): MAIN(:01), IMPULSE(:02), halftp_monitor(*/5)
# removed — see sync/donchian/RETIRED_STREAMS_REPORT.md.
#
# Emit every 10 min, +10s (2026-06-19). WHY not just on the bar boundary: the directional
# entry-confirm gate (ENTRY_CONFIRM_BUF) defers a breakout's emission until price confirms its
# direction (favourable 0.5R first), which happens MID-period — minutes/tens-of-minutes after the
# bar close. A boundary-only cron (hourly / :00,:30) therefore only emits the confirmed signal on
# the NEXT boundary, so a signal that fired at 19:00 and confirmed at 19:09 didn't appear until
# 20:00. Running */10 (still +10s, so the boundary runs :00:10/:30:10 catch a freshly-closed bar)
# emits a signal within ~10 min of it confirming, on EVERY stream. Idempotent: canli.py dedups on
# (symbol, signal_time, direction, mode), so re-checking the same bar every 10 min never duplicates;
# the 1.5h lookback keeps a still-confirming bar in scope until it's emitted.
#
# DONCHIAN live emit (every 10 min) — Donchian(55) 1h breakout, ER>=0.35 strong-trend gate
#   (mode='donchian'). Telegram alert per new signal.
*/10 * * * * sleep 10 && cd $HOME/ict-trade && $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/donchian/canli.py --emit >> $HOME/ict-donchian.log 2>&1
# DONCHIAN 30m+4h HYBRID live emit (every 10 min) — 30m breakout confirmed by 4h trend direction
#   (mode='dch30_4h'). Best stream overall (+1106R / 2024-26).
*/10 * * * * sleep 10 && cd $HOME/ict-trade && $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/donchian/canli.py --emit --tf 30m --confirm-htf 4h >> $HOME/ict-donchian.log 2>&1
# DONCHIAN 30m+4h · 6R live emit (every 10 min) — same hybrid signals, wider 6R target
#   (mode='dch30_4h6'). MFE-validated: ~2x R/trade vs 4R, OOS-robust across 2024-26.
*/10 * * * * sleep 10 && cd $HOME/ict-trade && $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/donchian/canli.py --emit --tf 30m --confirm-htf 4h --rr 6 >> $HOME/ict-donchian.log 2>&1
# Daily resolve -> the REALISTIC ·0.5R UI versions (the only ones the UI shows). The non-
#   conservative twins (donchian/dch30_4h/dch30_4h6/d30_4h_so) were removed from the UI, so they
#   are no longer resolved. DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 shifts the entry to the +0.5R confirm level and
#   auto-tags rows with a 'c' suffix; DCH_SO_RUNNER_CAP picks the scale-out runner cap.
# 00:30 — full-TP donchianc / dch30_4hc / dch30_4h6c  +  scale-out d30_4h_soc (cap=4, default).
#         Also self-heals the live table (prune_live drops signals that failed dir-confirm).
30 0 * * * cd $HOME/ict-trade && DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/sync_daily.py --stream all >> $HOME/ict-sync.log 2>&1
# 00:45 — scale-out 6R cap (same dch30_4h signals, wider runner) -> d30so6c.
45 0 * * * cd $HOME/ict-trade && DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 DCH_SO_RUNNER_CAP=6 $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/sync_daily.py --stream d30_4h_so >> $HOME/ict-sync.log 2>&1
# 01:00 — scale-out 8R cap -> d30so8c.
0 1 * * * cd $HOME/ict-trade && DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 DCH_SO_RUNNER_CAP=8 $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/sync_daily.py --stream d30_4h_so >> $HOME/ict-sync.log 2>&1
